Feature addition: taper pickup drop rates by difficulty level.

This commit modifies 4 files (+154/-6 lines), spanning 2 TypeScript source, 2 core game loop.
This feature extends the Geometry Wars 3D codebase with new functionality. The implementation follows the project's established patterns and maintains compatibility with both single-player and multiplayer code paths where applicable.

Additional context from the commit body:
- PickupSpawner: add setDifficultyLevel(level) + computeDropMultiplier()
  - diff 0-4: multiplier = 1.0 (full rates)
  - diff 4-8: linear taper 1.0 → 0.5
  - diff 8-12: linear taper 0.5 → 0.25
  - diff 12+: floor at 0.20
  - Base rate constants stored separately; effective rates computed from them
- BuffManager.rollBuffDrop(): add optional multiplier param (default 1.0)
- main.ts: call pickupSpawner.setDifficultyLevel(waveScheduler.currentDifficultyLevel) each frame
- Add unit tests: PickupSpawner.test.ts covering all acceptance criteria

Key files: src/buffs/BuffManager.ts, src/core/PickupSpawner.test.ts, src/core/PickupSpawner.ts, src/main.ts.
